@git
Feature: Git Fixtures
  Git fixture steps create disposable repositories for CLI smoke tests.

  @clean
  Scenario: creates a clean repository on main
    Given a git repository "repo" exists
    When I run "git -C repo branch --show-current"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then stdout equals "main"
    Then git repository "repo" is clean
    Then git repository "repo" has branch "main"

  @clean
  Scenario: committed file creates a repository
    Given git repository "repo" has committed file "README.md" with content:
      hello
    When I run "git -C repo show HEAD:README.md"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then stdout equals "hello"
    Then git repository "repo" is clean

  @dirty
  Scenario: untracked file makes repository dirty
    Given git repository "repo" has untracked file "scratch.txt" with content:
      dirty
    When I run "git -C repo status --porcelain"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "?? scratch.txt"
    Then git repository "repo" is dirty

  @dirty
  Scenario: modified tracked file makes repository dirty
    Given git repository "repo" has committed file "README.md" with content:
      old
    Given git repository "repo" has modified file "README.md" with content:
      new
    When I run "git -C repo status --porcelain"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "M README.md"
    Then git repository "repo" is dirty

  @branch
  Scenario: branch setup creates branch
    Given a git repository "repo" exists
    Given git repository "repo" is on branch "feature/test"
    When I run "git -C repo branch --show-current"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then stdout equals "feature/test"
    Then git repository "repo" has branch "feature/test"
